165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 104 0 R
/E (V-JEPA as 'eyes on the whole frame' helps find a target that has left the frame: ORR_all +1.9 over the baseline. The V-JEPA predictor is useful as an early warning that an occlusion is starting, and it makes the warning safer than one based on OSTrack's score alone: +0.64 AUC. The main open problem is the tracker confidently drifting onto a distractor before the occlusion even starts: OSTrack, acting as the judge, is fooled itself, so the next step is a judge that takes the world model into account.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
